<title>POLAND: Rafako dips on expected poor earnings.</title>
<headline>Rafako dips on expected poor earnings.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish industrial boilermaker Rafako SA fell 9.8 percent to 19.4 zlotys in a 1.1-million- zloty turnover, possibly in anticipation of disappointing earnings for September due on Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>Some said, however, the fall might be accidental given the relatively small turnover.</p>
<p>&quot;Maybe it's an expectation of poor earnings, although the management promised better earnings in the second half of the year than in the first one. But the fall might be simply accidental,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
